#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:10
msgid ""
"XNote is a sticky note application that strives to be simple, fault-"
"tolerant, and customizable. XNote consists of independent pad windows; each "
"is basically a text box in which notes can be written."
msgstr ""

#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:17
msgid "XNote contributors"
msgstr ""

#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:23
msgid ""
"Full rename from Xpad to XNote: new binary (xnote), package name, config "
"directory (~/.config/xnote), icons, and desktop integration. Existing notes "
"are automatically migrated from ~/.config/xpad on first launch. The package "
"replaces the old xpad package."
msgstr ""

#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:28
msgid ""
"Backup pipeline heartbeat and hardening, honest save-error handling, tray "
"watcher re-registration with a properly themable symbolic icon, and "
"packaging fixes (deb epoch, renderer pin moved into the binary, autostart as "
"a symlink)."
msgstr ""

#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:33
msgid ""
"Right-clicking a note now shows xpad's own menu (with Close) instead of the "
"text widget's built-in one, and Close is also available while text is "
"selected."
msgstr ""

#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:38
msgid ""
"New pads now pick a random classic sticky-note color (toggleable in "
"Preferences), and the Preferences Close button works again."
msgstr ""

#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:43
msgid ""
"The pad toolbar is now a floating rounded pill that fades in over the note "
"on hover, with symbolic icons and a corner resize grip."
msgstr ""

#: data/xnote.appdata.xml.in:48
msgid ""
"First XNote release: ported from GTK 3 to GTK 4 and libadwaita, with a "
"StatusNotifierItem tray and a symbolic top-bar icon."
msgstr ""
